      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to substitute the given values of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) into the expression \\(2a + 3b\\).\n\nFirst, let's identify the given values:\n\\[ a = 2 - i \\]\n\\[ b = -1 + i \\]\n\nNext, we substitute these values into the expression \\(2a + 3b\\):\n\n\\[ 2a + 3b = 2(2 - i) + 3(-1 + i) \\]\n\nNow, we will distribute the constants 2 and 3 into their respective terms:\n\n\\[ 2(2 - i) = 2 \\cdot 2 - 2 \\cdot i = 4 - 2i \\]\n\\[ 3(-1 + i) = 3 \\cdot -1 + 3 \\cdot i = -3 + 3i \\]\n\nNow, we add these two results together:\n\n\\[ 4 - 2i - 3 + 3i \\]\n\nCombine the real parts and the imaginary parts separately:\n\n\\[ (4 - 3) + (-2i + 3i) = 1 + i \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1 + i}\n\\]",
